---
interface Props {
  worksCount: number;
}

const { worksCount } = Astro.props;
// Editorial adaptation of the user-provided FLIPSART booklet.
---

<section class="art-intro" aria-labelledby="art-series-title">
  <div class="intro-topline fs-meta">
    <span>02 / Art</span>
    <span class="text-[var(--fs-mute)]">The FLIPSART archive</span>
  </div>

  <div class="intro-layout">
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p class="fs-meta-muted">From the world around the records</p>
      <h1 id="art-series-title" class="series-title">
        <span>The record ends.</span>
        <span>The image remains.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="intro-lead">The record was only the beginning.</p>
      <p class="intro-description">
        FLIPSART grew out of FLIPSIGHT’s sleeves, posters and visual experiments.
        Images made around house music, taken beyond their first purpose
        and given a life of their own on canvas.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-signals font-mono" aria-label="The origins of the series">
        <span>Sleeves</span><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Posters</span><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Side works</span>
      </p>

      <div class="intro-actions">
        <a class="intro-action-link works-link" href="#art-works">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M10 3v14m-6-6 6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="square" />
          </svg>
          <span>Explore the {worksCount} works</span>
        </a>
        <div>
          <a
            class="intro-action-link booklet-link"
            href="https://www.fldr.be/flagrant/preview-booklet-flipsart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            aria-describedby="booklet-link-meta"
          >
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M8 3h9v9M17 3 3 17" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="square" />
            </svg>
            <span>View PDF booklet</span>
          </a>
          <p id="booklet-link-meta" class="booklet-meta">Opens in a new tab</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="intro-figure">
      <div class="archive-image">
        <img
          src="/media/art/flipsart-origin-zigzag-2024.jpg"
          alt="A FLIPSIGHT Cafe poster on the glass door of Zigzag Records, alongside record sleeves and a synthesizer artwork in the window."
          width="1122"
          height="1402"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="caption-index" aria-hidden="true">↳</span>
        <span>FLIPSIGHT Cafe poster<br /><span class="text-[var(--fs-mute)]">15 June 2024</span></span>
        <span class="caption-archive">From the archive</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <details class="art-story" open>
    <summary>
      <span class="story-summary-label">
        <span class="fs-meta-muted">Behind the images</span>
        <span class="story-invitation">How a sleeve becomes a world of its own.</span>
      </span>
      <span class="story-toggle">
        <span class="story-label-closed">Read the story</span>
        <span class="story-label-open">Close the story</span>
        <svg class="story-toggle-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3 10h14M10 3v14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" />
        </svg>
      </span>
    </summary>

    <div class="story-content">
      <div class="story-chapters">
        <section aria-labelledby="art-story-origin">
          <p class="fs-meta-muted">01 / Origin</p>
          <h2 id="art-story-origin">Made around music.</h2>
          <p>
            FLIPSIGHT is an independent Antwerp label built around house music,
            visual identity and vinyl culture. From the start, every release
            needed its own image, atmosphere and physical presence.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some FLIPSART works began as sleeves, posters or event visuals.
            Others emerged as side works during the visual exploration around
            a release. Taken out of that first context, the image could become
            an artwork in its own right.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="art-story-tension">
          <p class="fs-meta-muted">02 / A different sense of time</p>
          <h2 id="art-story-tension">Future sound. Another time.</h2>
          <p>
            Synthesizers, turntables and studio equipment inhabit interiors
            and landscapes that feel slower, older and more painterly than
            the electronic music they refer to.
          </p>
          <p>
            That tension is The Future in Reverse: future-facing music culture
            pulled back into images that feel nostalgic, domestic or almost
            classical. The world of the club and the machine, seen through
            a different lens.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="art-story-process">
          <p class="fs-meta-muted">03 / From image to object</p>
          <h2 id="art-story-process">A new life on canvas.</h2>
          <p>
            Each work is built through concept, art direction and extensive
            manual refinement, with technology as a starting point.
            The image is not simply generated. It is built.
          </p>
          <p>
            More than enlarged covers, FLIPSART is a visual archive of
            FLIPSIGHT’s first three years: sleeves, posters, studies and
            side works given a new form as physical canvas pieces.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <blockquote>
        “The images still carry the atmosphere of the music,<br class="hidden md:block" />
        but they no longer need the music to exist.”
      </blockquote>
      <p class="story-credit fs-meta-muted">From the FLIPSART booklet / The Future in Reverse</p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

<style>
  .intro-topline {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fs-line-soft);
  }

  .intro-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(36px, 7vw, 112px);
    padding-block: clamp(36px, 4vw, 64px);
  }

  .intro-copy { padding-block: 12px; }
  .series-title {
    margin-top: 26px;
    font-family: var(--fs-display);
    font-size: clamp(40px, 4.5vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .series-title > span { display: block; text-wrap: balance; }
  .intro-lead {
    margin-top: 30px;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.55vw, 24px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro-description {
    max-width: 460px;
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--fs-ink-2);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .intro-signals {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    color: var(--fs-mute);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .intro-actions {
    display: grid;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .intro-action-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding-block: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fs-ink);
    font-family: var(--fs-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: color 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease;
  }
  .intro-action-link:hover { color: var(--fs-accent); border-color: var(--fs-accent); }
  .intro-action-link svg { flex-shrink: 0; }
  .booklet-meta { margin-top: 8px; padding-left: 30px; color: var(--fs-mute); font-family: var(--fs-mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .intro-action-link:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--fs-accent); outline-offset: 6px; }

  .intro-figure { width: 100%; max-width: 390px; justify-self: end; }
  .archive-image { background: var(--fs-bg-2); }
  .archive-image img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  figcaption {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-family: var(--fs-mono);
    font-size: 9px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .caption-index { font-size: 15px; }
  .caption-archive { margin-left: auto; color: var(--fs-mute); font-size: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }

  .art-story { border-block: 1px solid var(--fs-line); }
  summary { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; padding-block: 24px; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .story-summary-label { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px 28px; }
  .story-invitation { font-size: 16px; }
  .story-toggle { display: flex; flex-shrink: 0; align-items: center; gap: 20px; font-family: var(--fs-mono); font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  summary:hover .story-toggle { color: var(--fs-accent); }
  .story-label-open { display: none; }
  details[open] .story-label-closed { display: none; }
  details[open] .story-label-open { display: inline; }
  .story-toggle-icon { transition: transform 180ms ease; }
  details[open] .story-toggle-icon { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .story-content { border-top: 1px solid var(--fs-line-soft); padding-block: 40px; }
  .story-chapters { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 64px); }
  .story-chapters h2 { margin: 16px 0; font-size: 23px; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.025em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .story-chapters h2 ~ p { margin-top: 14px; color: var(--fs-ink-2); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; }
  blockquote { margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 34px; border-top: 1px solid var(--fs-line-soft); font-family: "Instrument Serif", Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(28px, 3.3vw, 48px); line-height: 1.16; text-wrap: balance; }
  .story-credit { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 9px; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .intro-layout { gap: 36px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .series-title { font-size: clamp(34px, 4.3vw, 40px); }
    .caption-archive { display: none; }
    .story-summary-label { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
    .story-chapters { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .story-chapters section { max-width: 680px; }
    .story-chapters section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--fs-line-soft); padding-top: 28px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .intro-topline { font-size: 9px; }
    .intro-layout { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; padding-block: 30px; }
    .intro-copy { padding: 0; }
    .intro-copy > .fs-meta-muted { font-size: 9px; }
    .series-title { margin-top: 22px; font-size: clamp(40px, 9.8vw, 62px); }
    .intro-lead { margin-top: 22px; }
    .intro-description { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
    .intro-signals { margin-top: 20px; }
    .intro-actions { margin-top: 18px; }
    .intro-figure { max-width: none; }
    .archive-image img { max-height: 420px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 57%; }
    .caption-archive { display: block; }
    summary { gap: 16px; padding-block: 22px; align-items: flex-start; }
    .story-invitation { max-width: 225px; font-size: 15px; }
    .story-toggle { gap: 10px; font-size: 9px; }
    .story-toggle-icon { margin-top: 3px; }
    .story-content { padding-block: 30px; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .story-toggle-icon, .intro-action-link { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
